      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Adaptation of https://github.com/axiomgraph/ComfyUIWorkflow/blob/main/Mage%20Flow%20Edit.json created by axiomgraph, with the sampler settings from https://github.com/starsFriday/ComfyUI-MageFlow and https://github.com/zhaotututu/ComfyUI-MageFlow.\n\n### No custom node needed\n\nComfyUI ships Mage-Flow support in core — `comfy/ldm/mage_flow`, the `mage` CLIP type and `TextEncodeMageFlowEdit` — so this runs on stock loaders. The community packs add convenience wrappers (an all-in-one loader) or a Diffusers-directory path that pulls in `diffusers` plus Microsoft's pinned source; neither buys anything core does not already do, so neither is installed.\n\n### Mage-Flow Edit Turbo\n\nThe distilled model: 4 steps at CFG 1.0, euler / simple. Roughly seven times faster than the 30-step model for a small quality cost.\n\n⚠ Keep `weight_dtype` at `bf16`. Activation-quantized FP8 (`fp8_e4m3fn_fast`) collapses Turbo's four-step result to noise on current ComfyUI/PyTorch CUDA builds — reported by starsFriday, and the reason the bf16 build is provisioned rather than an fp8 one.\n\nIf you replace a checkpoint under the same filename, restart ComfyUI: the model cache keys on the path, not the contents.\n\n### Model links\n\n```dotenv\nCOMFY_ASSET_PROFILES=mage-flow-edit-turbo\n```\n\nEverything comes from [Comfy-Org/Mage-Flow](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Mage-Flow), ungated. The profile downloads them; this template deliberately does not carry `properties.models`, because a 16 GB ungated stack should not land on every container that happens to have the templates installed.\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/models/\n├── 📂 diffusion_models/mage_flow_edit_turbo_bf16.safetensors\n├── 📂 text_encoders/qwen3vl_4b_bf16.safetensors\n└── 📂 vae/mage_flow_vae_bf16.safetensors\n```\n\nAlready running a `krea-2-*` profile? Point the CLIP loader at the 4.9 GB `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors` you already have instead of the 8.3 GB bf16 file — same Qwen3-VL-4B encoder, and the `mage` type applies the prompt template either way.\n\n### Why there is no NVFP4 build here\n\nThe `ajh-code/Mage-Flow-NVFP4-*` repos are standalone Diffusers pipelines shipping prebuilt `libmage_nvfp4_linear.so` CUDA kernels, not safetensors ComfyUI can load. The smallest ComfyUI-loadable builds are Comfy-Org's official `int8_convrot` quants at 3.9 GB — pick the `mage-flow-edit-int8` / `mage-flow-edit-turbo-int8` profile for those.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Credit, models and settings",
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
